# Third-party specifications we read but do not redistribute (Damian,
# 2026-09-07). Named file by file, NOT as docs/Reference/*.pdf: that
# directory IS published and carries other third-party PDFs whose terms
# allow it. Until this rule existed the reconcile in PublicPush.md 2b
# proposed all ten on every run and nothing but prose withheld them.
# docs/Reference/CONTENTS.md is published and names each one with a link
# to its public source, so a reader can see what is withheld and fetch it.
docs/Reference/HID_1_11_Specification.pdf
docs/Reference/HID_1_11_Specification.txt
docs/Reference/Intel_82583V_Datasheet.pdf
docs/Reference/Intel_82583V_Datasheet.txt
docs/Reference/Intel_I219_Datasheet.pdf
docs/Reference/Intel_I219_Datasheet.txt
docs/Reference/USB_2_0_Specification.pdf
docs/Reference/USB_2_0_Specification.txt
docs/Reference/xHCI_Specification.pdf
docs/Reference/xHCI_Specification.txt

# Sitting configs name the box they were built to interrogate (one line is
# 'b3 peer=192.168.6.141:7 ip=192.168.6.200', Damian's LAN). PublicPush.md
# has said they never ship since Update 49; until this rule, nothing but
# that sentence withheld them, and the reconcile listed all seven on every
# run. build/check-shipping-images.ps1 keeps the same addresses off the
# shipping IMAGE; this keeps them off the cfg one file over.
build/boot/diag-sitting*.cfg
